notes:
LAN (Local Area Network) - Connects computers and other devices to a dedicated area like home, office or school.
LAN topologies:
  Star topology - Devices are connected individually via a central networking device such as a swith or hub.
    Pros - Reliable and scalable.
    Cons - Costs more than others, high maintenance, harder troubleshoot,
  Bus topology - Devices connected to a single cable known as the backbone cable.
    Pros - Cost-efficient.
    Cons - Prone to bottlenecks, becoming slow and harder troubleshoot.
  Ring topology - Devices connected to to eachother to form a loop
    Pros - Only one direction data can travel so easy to troubleshoot. Less prone to bottlenecks than bus topology.
    Cons - It isn't efficient.
Switch - Connect devices to the same network and allows data to travel by MAC addresses.
Hub - The worse switch. Sends the data to all devices connected.
Router - Connects netowrks and passes data between them. 
Subnetting - Splitting up a network into smaller, miniature networks within itself.
Subnet mask - 32-bit number in IPv4 networks to divide an IP address into two parts. The network portion and host (device) portion.
  Network address - Identifies the start of the actual network and is used to identify a network's existence.
  Host address - An IP address used to identify a device on the subnet.
  Default gateway - Special address assigned to a device on the network that is capablle of sending information to another network.

